  (:id "c/C9" :type :task :title "union tag past arms → None" :state :done :evidence
   ("https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/pull/1255: the union_tag_both_plans row on c, both plans"
    "internal/codegen/ctable/fixedversioning_union_tag_both_plans_test.go: TestFixedVersioningUnionTagBothPlans"
    "merged into fixed-table-form at 68da39fca2d898f876587724b216530a19f955c7") :audit-item "C9"
   :reported-state "implemented-asserted" :reported-source
   "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/898#issuecomment-5648020292" :note
   "Reconciled 2026-09-19 under Glenn ruling of the same day: done means everything is tested and verified working. The single clause of this title — a union tag past the arm set lands None — is tested on BOTH read paths by the union_tag_both_plans row in :evidence. The forge sets the one-byte pick.type tag of old_union_append.bin to 9, past the OLD writer two arms and the NEW reader three, located by a nine-byte needle asserted to occur EXACTLY ONCE before the write, and the same bytes are then read by the COMPILED plan and by the IDENTITY plan; both must land None. This row was cut because the bound was guarded by NOTHING: the shift deleted the union tag bound from the emitter of all nine legs and not one landed fixed-table test went red. A separate question is OPEN and is NOT part of this clause: over the same bytes the two plans disagree about the clamped COUNTER on several legs (schema#1254). This task is about the LANDING, which both plans agree on.")
  (:id "c/C10" :type :task :title "enum ordinal past top → None" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t06_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCT06Bounds/c/C10" "docs/roadmap-evidence/fixed-c.sexp at 86701e728868 on sprint/schema-finish: this task's done form, landed by land schema-c-t06-bounds (sprint stream schema-c)") :audit-item "C10" :reported-state "implemented-asserted" :reported-source "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/898#issuecomment-5648020292" :note "Done 2026-10-11 from its landed evidence form: tested at 7aee80d8d10a, landed on sprint/schema-finish at 86701e728868 (card schema-c-t06-bounds). The code and the test are on sprint/schema-finish; main carries them once that branch merges. Earlier note: Historical report at b7ab66a8; current completion has not been reconciled." :tested-revision "7aee80d8d10a2b9b89d4c3a04f0552686057939c" :landed-revision "86701e728868db3bf921a6f21e42d80c8db3f890")
  (:id "c/R31" :type :task :title "full-width lanes: arg/arg2 full width in the emitted static plan with the compare at the tag's own width; a 64-bit ordinal temporary; the remap table as long as the WRITER's variant count, refusing by name past the length word" :state :unknown :evidence nil :audit-item "R31" :reported-state "implemented-asserted" :reported-source "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/898#issuecomment-5648020292" :note "Open, v1.3 (2026-10-11): card schema-c-t06-bounds landed on sprint/schema-finish at 86701e728868 with this task unknown: the remap table as long as the WRITER's variant count, refusing by name past the length word (§5.8 row 14) is unproved: no test in the tree builds a writer with more than 255 variants, and the in-package test asserts the shared runtime template's full-width arg/arg2, argw and 64-bit ordinal temporary, not a compiled plan's remap table past 255 entries Earlier note: Historical report at b7ab66a8; current completion has not been reconciled." :sprint-card "schema-c-t06-bounds" :release "v1.3")
