  (:id "cs/C9" :type :task :title "union tag past arms → None" :state :unknown :evidence ("no union_tag_both_plans row has landed on cs: the eighth shift wrote it, gated it green and HELD it because control 3 came back green" "the card is at schema8/cs_utbp_test.go.card") :audit-item "C9" :reported-state "implemented-asserted" :reported-source "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/898#issuecomment-5650042470" :note "Open, v1.3 (2026-10-11): carried by sprint card schema-cs-t06-bounds (review, attempt 7), last pushed head bb6bdfa6b89cadf735766ef9fce72ec9f4a5f592 on sprint/schema-cs-t06-bounds.w7.g2.e17; open finding: broken — R31's title clause \"the remap table as long as the WRITER's variant count, refusing by name past the length word\" is unasserted (fixedroadmap_t06_test.go:224-229) and unimplemented (fixedruntime.go:790 still caps at 255), yet fixed-cs.sexp:76 records cs/R31 :state :done. / The coordinator's arg2 gap is resolved: `TableFixedEntry` carries `Guard2`/`Arg2`/`ArgW2` / (internal/codegen/cstable/fixedruntime.go:39- ... Earlier note: NOT reconciled, and nothing landed. The eighth shift WROTE the union_tag_both_plans row for cs, gated it green and then HELD it rather than open it, because its decisive control came back GREEN: cutting the emitter union tag bound leaves 71 leaves and 0 red, and so does cutting the tag clamp in fixedbounds.go. The cs runtime case Const: passes the CONSTANT and never the file raw tag, so the bound cannot fire for the None case — possibly dead code. A row whose decisive control is green proves nothing, and the shift was right to report it rather than commit it. The card is at schema8/cs_utbp_test.go.card and is the next shift first job." :sprint-card "schema-cs-t06-bounds" :release "v1.3")
